## §4 State & `__init__` [mixed]

| ID | Sev | Rule | Verdict | Evidence (file:line) | Note |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| R4.1 | **CRITICAL** | No module-level global mutable state, and no singleton used to dodge DI for a collaborator that can vary (`PLW0603` + DI principle) | | | |
| R4.1a | STANDARD | Frozen, load-once startup constant (e.g. `Settings`) may be a module singleton - but check the 4-point bright-line test and confirm access stays injected, not `imported` | | | |
| R4.2 | **CRITICAL** | No logic in `__init__` - attribute assignment only; move I/O / API / parsing / heavy compute to a `@classmethod` factory | | | |
| R4.3 | STANDARD | Instantiate at point of use, or cache on the owning object; inject boundary collaborators (DB/HTTP/AWS) as constructor params | | | |

## §5 Classes & naming [REVIEW]

| ID | Sev | Rule | Verdict | Evidence (file:line) | Note |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| R5.1 | STANDARD | Group into a class when it earns its instance (real state / injected collaborator / substitutable abstraction); no all-`@staticmethod` "utility class"; don't wrap one trivial helper. *(provisional - pending coding-patterns re-sign-off)* | | | |
| R5.2 | **CRITICAL** | Auto-explicative code - names carry meaning; a reviewer understands intent without comments; prefer renaming over commenting | | | |
| R5.3 | STANDARD | Everything the code says is in English - identifiers, comments, docstrings, log messages, user-/LLM-facing output; only genuine domain proper nouns stay in the domain language | | | |
| R5.4 | STANDARD | Access data by field name, not index, when both are available | | | |
| R5.5 | STANDARD | No `getattr` / `setattr` - explicit attribute access (`hasattr` is fine). | | | |
| R5.6 | STANDARD | Blank line before and after a conditional block (skip the leading blank line for a first-statement guard clause). | | | |
| R5.7 | STANDARD | Code speaks capability language - no initiative codenames, work-item numbers, sprint/phase labels or planning jargon in identifiers, comments, docstrings, or test names; traceability = commit message + PR work-item link. See "Repo adaptations" above for the ADR/issue-citation exception. | | | |
| R5.8 | STANDARD | No term borrowed from another trade meaning - every identifier checked against its established industry meaning (`profile` = performance profiling, so column/dtype/null inspection is `discover_structure`) | | | |
| R5.9 | STANDARD | A `Protocol` in production code earns its place only as a runtime substitution seam - 2+ real implementations swapped at runtime (shipping or concretely planned). A test-only seam lives in the test suite; production annotates the concrete class (constructor injection unaffected - R4.3/§10). Not justified by a falsely "optional" dependency (R9.7); no `@runtime_checkable` without a real `isinstance` call; docstring names the implementations | | | |

